<h2 class="sub-heading" style="margin-top: 2rem;">Locally Owned. Regionally Trusted.</h2>
  <p class="p-home">
    Central Michigan isn't a single city or a single county—it's a stretch of the Lower Peninsula that runs from the 
    lakes and forests of Clare County in the north down through the agricultural heartland of Gratiot County in the south, 
    with Isabella County at the center and Mecosta County reaching west toward Big Rapids, and Midland County to the east. It's a region of small cities, 
    tight-knit towns, working farms, lakefront communities, and rural roads that connect them all. Isabella Garage Door 
    was built for exactly this territory. We're based in Rosebush—genuinely in the middle of it—and we service every 
    corner of Central Michigan with the same fast response, honest pricing, and quality work that our home community 
    has always expected from us.
  </p>
  <p class="p-home" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
    When you call us, you reach a real person who knows exactly where you are. Mt. Pleasant is minutes away. 
    Clare and Farwell are up Old 27. Alma and St. Louis are down US-127. Remus is west on M-20. We know these 
    corridors, these communities, and these people—not because we studied a map, but because this is home.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="core-services-section">
  <h2 class="sub-heading">Complete Garage Door Services Across Central Michigan</h2>
  <p class="core-services-intro">
    Every community in our service area gets access to the same full range of services. Here's what Central Michigan homeowners, farmers, and property owners count on us for:
  </p>

  <div class="core-services-grid">

    <a href="/services/broken-springs" class="core-services-card spring reveal-on-scroll">
      <h3>Broken Spring Replacement</h3>
      <p>Broken springs are the most common garage door failure in Central Michigan—and the most urgent. When a spring snaps, your door isn't moving safely until it's replaced. We carry high-cycle replacement springs for residential and agricultural applications, serve the entire region, and prioritize spring calls for same-day response wherever possible. We replace both springs at once and balance the door before we leave.</p>
    </a>

    <a href="/services/door-repair" class="core-services-card repair">
      <h3>General Door Repair</h3>
      <p>Off-track doors, snapped cables, worn rollers, bent tracks, damaged panels—we find the real problem and fix it. Central Michigan's housing stock ranges from century-old farmhouses to new construction subdivisions, and we've worked on garage hardware across the full spectrum. No configuration surprises us and no job gets a generic fix.</p>
    </a>

    <a href="/services/opener-repair" class="core-services-card opener">
      <h3>Opener Repair & Installation</h3>
      <p>Every opener brand, every failure mode—we've seen them all across the region. We service LiftMaster, Chamberlain, Genie, Craftsman, and all major brands. When repair isn't worth it, we install new smart openers with Wi-Fi and smartphone control. Especially valuable for rural properties and farm operations where remote access matters.</p>
    </a>
<!--
    <a href="/services/new-door-installation" class="core-services-card installation">
      <h3>New Door Installation</h3>
      <p>A new garage door is one of the highest-return home improvements available in Central Michigan's market. We install quality residential doors in every style—traditional, carriage house, modern—in steel, wood, or composite. Heavy-duty options for agricultural buildings and shops. We handle everything from measurement to removal of your old door to final adjustment throughout the region.</p>
    </a>
-->
    <a href="/services/maintenance" class="core-services-card maintenance">
      <h3>Preventive Maintenance</h3>
      <p>Central Michigan winters are real—cold that tightens springs, moisture that corrodes hardware, and freeze-thaw cycles that wear on every moving part. An annual tune-up before the season turns keeps your entire system running reliably and catches problems while they're still inexpensive. Available throughout the service area, residential and agricultural.</p>
    </a>
