<section style="margin-top: 2rem;">
  <h2 class="sub-heading">Every Community in Our Service Area</h2>
  <p class="p-home">
    We've built dedicated service pages for each community in our area because we believe every town deserves to be
    treated as its own place—not a line item on a regional coverage map. Here's where we work, and what makes each community worth knowing:
  </p>

  <div class="p-home" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">

    <p><strong>📍 <a href="/locations/mt-pleasant" style="color: #b27d57;">Mt. Pleasant</a></strong><br>
    The commercial and civic hub of Isabella County—our most frequently served city. CMU drives a large rental market alongside established residential neighborhoods and a busy south side. Minutes from our Rosebush base and one of our fastest response areas in the region.</p>

    <p style="margin-top: 1rem;"><strong>📍 <a href="/locations/rosebush" style="color: #b27d57;">Rosebush</a></strong><br>
    Home base. Isabella Garage Door is based right here in Rosebush—which means Rosebush and Isabella Township properties get the fastest possible response. When you call from Rosebush, you're calling your actual neighbor.</p>

    <p style="margin-top: 1rem;"><strong>📍 <a href="/locations/lake-isabella" style="color: #b27d57;">Lake Isabella</a></strong><br>
    One of Isabella County's premier lakefront communities—a mix of year-round residents and seasonal cottage owners spread across Broomfield, Rolland, and Coe Township. We service lakefront homes, year-round neighborhoods, and seasonal properties throughout the lake community.</p>

    <p style="margin-top: 1rem;"><strong>📍 <a href="/locations/beal-city" style="color: #b27d57;">Beal City</a></strong><br>
    A tight-knit faith-and-farming community in Denver Township, just minutes from our Rosebush base. Multigenerational farms, well-kept homes, and one of the most closely connected communities in Isabella County. The Aggies country—and we know every road in it.</p>

    <p style="margin-top: 1rem;"><strong>📍 <a href="/locations/shepherd" style="color: #b27d57;">Shepherd</a></strong><br>
    Home of the Maple Syrup Festival and the Bluejays, sitting right at the Isabella-Gratiot county line. We cover both sides of the line without hesitation—Coe Township on the Isabella side, Gratiot County properties to the south and east.</p>

    <p style="margin-top: 1rem;"><strong>📍 <a href="/locations/clare" style="color: #b27d57;">Clare</a></strong><br>
    The Gateway to Michigan's North—where Old 27 meets US-10 and half of lower Michigan stops for gas and a dozen from Cops &amp; Doughnuts. About 20 minutes up Old 27 from Rosebush. Strong rural coverage into Clare County beyond the city.</p>

    <p style="margin-top: 1rem;"><strong>📍 <a href="/locations/farwell" style="color: #b27d57;">Farwell</a></strong><br>
    Clare's neighbor across the Muskegon River—its own distinct community with its own neighborhoods and rural roads reaching into northern Clare County. About 25 minutes up Old 27 from Rosebush, and we treat Farwell as a destination, not a detour.</p>

    <p style="margin-top: 1rem;"><strong>📍 <a href="/locations/alma" style="color: #b27d57;">Alma</a></strong><br>
    The Gratiot County seat—home of Alma College, the Highland Festival, and some of the best-preserved older homes in mid-Michigan. About 20 minutes south on US-127. We're experienced with Alma's older housing stock and know the difference between a Pine River address and a Wright Avenue one.</p>

    <p style="margin-top: 1rem;"><strong>📍 <a href="/locations/st-louis" style="color: #b27d57;">St. Louis</a></strong><br>
    The geographic center of Michigan's Lower Peninsula—and well within the center of our service area. About 25 minutes south on US-127. St. Louis gets its own service, not Alma's overflow—we know which side of the Pine River we're heading to.</p>

    <p style="margin-top: 1rem;"><strong>📍 <a href="/locations/coleman" style="color: #b27d57;">Coleman</a></strong><br>
    Comets country—a working-class farming community on M-18 between Mt. Pleasant and Midland, with strong agricultural roots in Midland County. Pole barns and farm doors are a big part of our work in the Coleman area, and we come prepared for them.</p>

    <p style="margin-top: 1rem;"><strong>📍 <a href="/locations/remus" style="color: #b27d57;">Remus</a></strong><br>
    Home of the Wheatland Music Festival and surrounded by the farm country of Wheatland Township in Mecosta County. About 20 minutes west on M-20. Remus isn't our edge case—it's a regular stop on a route we know well.</p>

  </div>

